---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us – Independent Craft & Philosophy"
  description={`Learn about ${siteConfig.name}, our privacy-first philosophy, zero-tracking architecture, and the handcrafted Living Clock art installation.`}
  path="/about/"
>
  <article class="content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Independent Craft & Philosophy</p>
    <h1>About {siteConfig.name}</h1>

    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} was created to solve a quiet frustration with the modern web: basic utility
      tools like clocks, stopwatches, and timers have become bloated with intrusive popups, battery-draining
      trackers, and laggy frameworks. We believe that everyday instruments should be fast, aesthetically pleasing,
      and strictly respectful of your personal attention.
    </p>

    <h2>The Three Core Principles</h2>
    <p>
      Every instrument on {siteConfig.name} is designed around three non-negotiable principles:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>100% Client-Side Privacy:</strong> No accounts, no user profiles, and no background telemetry.
        Your timer presets, alarm configurations, and saved world cities never leave your personal browser.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Zero-Drift Mathematical Precision:</strong> Instead of relying on naive intervals that drift
        when browser tabs throttle, our tools continuously synchronize against hardware monotonic clocks
        (<code>performance.now()</code>) and native IANA time zone definitions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Instant Static Architecture:</strong> Built on Astro with zero runtime JavaScript framework overhead,
        delivering sub-millisecond render times and complete offline readiness via modern Service Workers.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Living Clock: Art That Breathes With Time</h2>
    <p>
      Unlike cold digital displays, time in nature is fluid, atmospheric, and rhythmic. That insight led to the
      creation of our signature <strong>Living Clock</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Rather than generic stock illustrations, each Living Clock scene (such as <em>The Lantern Island</em>,
      <em>Moonlit Conservatory</em>, and <em>Rainlight Window</em>) is handcrafted using 3D modeling in Blender
      and procedural canvas shaders. The ambient sunlight warms at dawn, deepens at dusk, and transitions into
      gentle starlight at night—reflecting the natural progression of your local day without demanding your attention.
    </p>

    <h2>Technical Transparency & Standards</h2>
    <p>
      All date and time transformations leverage the standardized ECMAScript <code>Intl</code> API and the canonical
      IANA (Olson) Time Zone Database. When daylight saving transitions create non-existent spring hours or duplicated
      autumn hours, our converter algorithms explicitly alert you and preserve your disambiguated choice in shareable links.
    </p>

    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} is an independent, engineer-crafted web project. We take pride in building software that
      respects human focus and operates as a quiet digital companion for your desk, study sessions, and daily routines.
      If you have suggestions, questions, or bug reports, please reach out to us on our
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
